  "plain": "In the 1950s there may have been a programme to hand out material recovered from crashed craft to the government-funded research centres called FFRDCs (federally funded research and development centres). The idea is that this material sped up and inspired new technology. Michels raises this himself as something he wonders about, agreeing with what the online researcher UAPGerb had just said, and with the late Army officer Philip J. Corso also named in the conversation. If true, some modern technology would trace back to retrieved non-human material."
